                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a84adaaa-0d97-3de7-a9e6-29f0ab72b818",
                        "entry_id": "03953ed2-b3f7-3c5a-bc8d-61b56f40aa5b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fabelwesen, das zur Hälfte Greif und zur anderen Hälfte Pferd ist"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3dc5289-4808-4774-828a-d6587d10c8cf",
                                "sense_id": "a84adaaa-0d97-3de7-a9e6-29f0ab72b818",
                                "text": "„Personen, die sie rochen, neigten dazu, kurzzeitig gewaltige Landschaften zu sehen, voller eigenartiger Hügel oder endloser Alleen, gesäumt von Sphinxen und Hippogryphen, die sich bis zum Horizont erstreckten.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d3715e6-017b-401f-ad19-9ee01d6fc287",
                        "source_entry_id": "03953ed2-b3f7-3c5a-bc8d-61b56f40aa5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "a84adaaa-0d97-3de7-a9e6-29f0ab72b818",
                        "source_sense_description": "Fabelwesen, das zur Hälfte Greif und zur anderen Hälfte Pferd ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "駿鷹",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4695c594-d68a-465a-949c-d566ec479d30",
                        "source_entry_id": "03953ed2-b3f7-3c5a-bc8d-61b56f40aa5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "a84adaaa-0d97-3de7-a9e6-29f0ab72b818",
                        "source_sense_description": "Fabelwesen, das zur Hälfte Greif und zur anderen Hälfte Pferd ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "hippogriff",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hippogriff",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                        "entry_id": "c8369223-b411-3295-9155-844cd3f11038",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "a mythical beast, half griffin and half horse, supposedly the offspring of a griffin and a filly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ab2caa3-4bdb-4ceb-9fe1-604c501829a3",
                                                "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                                "text": "To talk of being able to ride with stirrups, is trifling: get on Pegasus, bestride the hippogryph, or mount the white nag in the Revelation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b844b8b7-26e2-4a5c-a771-ab0a70505e21",
                                                "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                                "text": "Je crains done qu'il faudra que nous nous contentions de quelque moyen plus simple et plus facile, comme d'un enchanteur à gages, un hippogriffe, ou au moins de quelque génie bienfaisant, …\nSo I doubt we must be content with some more simple and easy method, such as a magician in our pay, a hippogryph, or at least some kind genius, …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98afaba6-776e-41f4-9979-3a4377e2b4b5",
                                                "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                                "text": "Yet the work is surely not a mere map of the hippogryffon wanderings of some disordered imagination…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63364590-fa24-4dd6-ab81-d831b310d801",
                                                "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                                "text": "I imagine a Hippogryph. The Hippogryph is at once the object of the act and the act itself. Abstract the one, the other has no existence: deny me the consciousness of the Hippogryph, you deny me the consciousness of the imagination; I am conscious of zero; I am not conscious at all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a173cbf-c1e0-44d2-adda-5a4bbc6cb954",
                                                "sense_id": "74fb6417-dbb3-3f66-91e4-d8c35ec43ac6",
                                                "text": "Oceanus himself follows on a hippogriff, and counsels Prometheus to submit to Zeus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1516ea53-628d-427b-b382-cc2f9ca956c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "03953ed2-b3f7-3c5a-bc8d-61b56f40aa5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "a84adaaa-0d97-3de7-a9e6-29f0ab72b818",
                        "source_sense_description": "Fabelwesen, das zur Hälfte Greif und zur anderen Hälfte Pferd ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "hippogryph",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hippogryph",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "942fcccd-8286-36c9-9e31-3256dfc80e2e",
                                        "entry_id": "56f2cc97-61bd-3fb4-bfa2-0dbf2b29ed8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of hippogriff."
                                        ],
